<title>BELGIUM: AEA member cargo traffic up 4.4 pct in June.</title>
<headline>AEA member cargo traffic up 4.4 pct in June.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Association of European Airlines  (AEA) cargo figures for June 1997 show that total AEA member tonnage  carried in June was up 4.4 percent from June '96.</p>
<p>All of AEA's trade sectors experienced an increase except Europe-Sub  Saharan Africa which dipped by 3.7 percent to 146.2 million revenue  freight tonne kilometres (RFTK).</p>
<p>The largest increases were in the Europe to North Africa and Middle  East and the Mid Atlantic regions.</p>
<p>    Region			June 1997	  Pct Change</p>
<p>				    Million RFTK	on 1996</p>
<p>    Europe			    79.9	    UP    3.7</p>
<p>    Europe-N Africa/M East	 89.8	   UP   11.9</p>
<p>    North Atlantic		  761.9	   UP    4.8</p>
<p>    Europe-F. East/Australasia  792.7	   UP    4.2</p>
<p>    Europe-Sub Saharan Africa   146.2	   DOWN  3.7</p>
<p>    South Atlantic		  112.5	   UP    4.0</p>
<p>    Mid Atlantic		    105.9	   UP   11.3</p>
<p>    Total longhaul		1,919.5	   UP    4.2</p>
<p>    Total international	 2,089.2	   UP    4.4</p>
<p>*These figures relate to the international scheduled services of AEA  member airlines.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
